==Russian==

===Etymology 1===
From {{af|ru|по-|носи́ть}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ru-IPA|поноси́ть}}

====Verb====
{{ru-verb|поноси́ть|pf|impf=носи́ть}}

# {{lb|ru|transitive}} to [[carry]] something (for a while)
# {{lb|ru|transitive}} to [[wear]] clothes, to shoes (for a while)

=====Usage notes=====
{{U:sla:directional verb|ru|multi|impf=носи́ть|pf=поноси́ть|othimpf=нести́|othpf=понести́}}

=====Conjugation=====
{{ru-conj|pf|4c+p|поноси́ть}}

=====Synonyms=====
* {{l|ru|потаска́ть}}

=====Related terms=====
* {{l|ru|носи́ть}}

===Etymology 2===
Possibly from {{af|ru|поно́с|-и́ть}}. Unlikely from {{af|ru|по-|носи́ть}}, as {{m|ru|по-}} is almost always a perfectivizing prefix.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ru-IPA|поноси́ть}}

====Verb====
{{ru-verb|поноси́ть|impf}}

# {{lb|ru|transitive}} to [[vilify]], to [[criticize]], to [[insult]]
#: {{syn|ru|руга́ть|хули́ть|ха́ять}}

=====Conjugation=====
{{ru-conj|impf|4c|поноси́ть|ppp=-|prpp=+}}

===Etymology 3===
{{af|ru|поно́с|-ить}}

====Pronunciation====
* {{ru-IPA|поно́сить}}

====Verb====
{{ru-verb|поно́сить|impf}}

# {{lb|ru|impersonal}} to [[cause]] (bad) [[diarrhea]]
#: {{uxi|ru|[[он|его́]] '''поно́сит'''|he has bad diarrhea}}

=====Conjugation=====
{{ru-conj|impf-impers|4a|поно́сить}}

=====Related terms=====
* {{l|ru|поно́с|g=m}}
